# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# rustc silently normalizes CRLF away when it reads a source file; rust-analyzer's
# lexer does not, and rejects the bare CR inside a string literal. A CRLF checkout
# therefore turns every line-continuation ("...text \<newline>   more...") and every
# multi-line string in the codebase into a phantom "unknown character escape" /
# "Character must be escaped" error in the editor, with type-inference fallout
# downstream, while `cargo check` stays perfectly clean.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
